Common bupropion side effects:
The most common side effects may include:
dry mouth, sore throat, stuffy nose;
ringing in the ears;
blurred vision;
nausea, vomiting, stomach pain, loss of appetite, constipation;
sleep problems (insomnia);
tremors, sweating, feeling anxious or nervous;
fast heartbeats;
confusion, agitation, hostility;
rash;
weight loss;
increased urination;
headache, dizziness; or muscle or joint pain.
Serious bupropion side effects:
Get emergency medical help if you have any of these signs of an allergic reaction to bupropion: hives, itching, fever, swollen glands, difficult breathing, or swelling in your face or throat.
Get emergency medical help if you have a severe skin reaction to bupropion: fever, sore throat, burning eyes, skin pain, or a red or purple skin rash with blistering and peeling.
Report any new or worsening symptoms to your doctor.
Mood or behavior changes are new or worsening symptoms.
Anxiety is a new or worsening symptom.
Depression is a new or worsening symptom.
Panic attacks are new or worsening symptoms.

